---
title: Magic Chocolate Flan Cake
description: Chocolate cake and flan baked in one Bundt pan, where the layers trade places in the oven.
tags: [cake, baking]
course: dessert
icons: [cake-slice, custard, candy-bar]
source:
  name: Cook's Country
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/7229-magic-chocolate-flan-cake
servings: 16
time: 12h
---

= Cake

Adjust the oven rack to the middle position and heat the oven to 350°F (175°C).

Grease a 12-cup nonstick #Bundt pan{}.

Microwave the @caramel sauce{1/2%cup}(or topping, 118 ml) until easily pourable, about ~warm{30%seconds}. Pour into the pan to coat the bottom.

Combine the @all-purpose flour{89%g}(1/2 cup plus 2 tbsp), @cocoa{28%g}(1/3 cup), @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, and @salt{1/8%tsp} in a #bowl{}; set aside.

Combine the @bittersweet chocolate{113%g}(4 oz, chopped) and @unsalted butter{84%g}(6 tbsp) in a #large bowl{} and microwave at 50% power, stirring occasionally, until melted, ~melt{2-4%minutes}.

Whisk the @buttermilk{1/2%cup}(118 ml), @sugar{99%g}(1/2 cup), @eggs{2}(large), and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} into the chocolate mixture until incorporated.

Stir in the flour mixture until just combined. Pour the batter over the caramel in the prepared pan.

= Flan

Process the @sweetened condensed milk{2%can}(14 oz each), @whole milk{2 1/2%cup}(591 ml), @cream cheese{6%oz}(170 g), @&eggs{6}, @egg yolks{4}(large), and @&vanilla extract{1%tsp} in a #blender{} until smooth, about ~blend{1%minute}.

= Bake

Gently pour the flan over the cake batter in the Bundt pan and place the pan in a #large roasting pan{}.

Place the roasting pan on the oven rack and pour warm water into the roasting pan until it reaches halfway up the side of the Bundt pan.

Bake until a toothpick inserted in the cake comes out clean and the flan registers 180°F (82°C), ~bake{75-90%minutes}.

Transfer the Bundt pan to a #wire rack{}. Let cool to room temperature, about ~cool{2%hours}, then refrigerate until set, at least ~set{8%hours}. (Remove the roasting pan from the oven once the water has cooled.)

Set the bottom third of the Bundt pan in a bowl of hot tap water for ~loosen{1%minute}. Turn a completely flat #cake platter{} upside down over the pan, then gently flip the platter and pan together. Lift the pan off slowly and let the caramel run down over the cake. Serve.
